    "text": "```python\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\ndef parse_iso8601(s: str) -> datetime:\n    try:\n        if s.endswith('Z'):\n            return datetime.fromisoformat(s[:-1]).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n        elif '+' in s or '-' in s:\n            return datetime.fromisoformat(s)\n        else:\n            return datetime.fromisoformat(s).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    except ValueError:\n        raise ValueError(\"Unparseable ISO-8601 timestamp\")\n\n# Examples\n# parse_iso8601(\"2023-01-01T12:00:00Z\")  # UTC with trailing Z\n# parse_iso8601(\"2023-01-01T12:00:00+02:00\")  # Explicit offset\n# parse_iso8601(\"2023-01-01T12:00:00\")  # Naive timestamp, interpreted as UTC\n# parse_iso8601(\"2023-01-01 12:00:00\")  # Invalid format, raises ValueError\n```",
